.TH fleetring-dev-status 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-dev\-status \- Says whether the dev node runs, with its PID, address and release
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring dev status\fR [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Says whether the dev node runs, with its PID, address and release
.PP
It also names the node\*(Aqs log and context. Exits 0 either way.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<DATA_DIR>\fR
The dev directory; `~/.fleetring` by default
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
The output format: `table`, `json`, or `jsonl`

`table` is for people; `json` is one object with stable snake_case fields; `jsonl` is the same object on one line. A watch prints one object per line for either.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: For people: a table, or key and value lines for one item
.IP \(bu 2
json: For programs: one JSON object, indented
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl: For programs: one JSON object per line
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Short for `\-o json`
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
